# Native Qwen3-Omni thinker/VLM slice — notices and provenance

## Third-party code vendored in this directory

- `stb_image.h` — stb image decoder, v2.32, dual-licensed public domain
  (Unlicense) and MIT. Upstream: https://github.com/nothings/stb.
  Used only to decode JPEG/PNG/BMP input images. Only the JPEG/PNG/BMP
  decoders are compiled (`STBI_ONLY_*`). No modifications to the decoder
  logic; the header is vendored verbatim with its own license block.

## Code derived from the existing ASR slice (same repository, same license)

These primitives were adapted from `native/umm_asr_native/` (Apache-2.0,
original work in this repository) into `cuda_kernels_omni.*` and `bf16.hpp`,
keeping the SPDX header and changing only the namespace:

- RMSNorm / LayerNorm kernels, SiLU-mul, GELU (erf), residual add,
  fp32->bf16, embedding gather, row replace, argmax
- the GQA attention kernel (used for both text causal attention and the
  vision tower's bidirectional MHA with group size 1)

New CUDA primitives written for this slice: the text mRoPE and vision rotary
kernels, gelu_pytorch_tanh, the MoE router softmax/top-k, qkv strided split,
and deepstack scatter-add.

## Matmul kernels (rewritten 2026-11-17, still no copied source)

`omni_gemm.cu` replaces the previous 32x32 tiled BF16 GEMM, the naive
thread-per-output GEMM, the block-per-row GEMV and the single-block expert
GEMV accumulator. It contains four hand-written kernels: a tensor-core
`mma.sync.m16n8k16` GEMM with cp.async double buffering and `ldmatrix`
operand loads, a grouped (per-expert) variant of the same tile for MoE, a
warp-per-row 16-byte-load GEMV for batch-1 decode, and the pair-order MoE
combine. These are original work for this repository under Apache-2.0.

No third-party CUDA source was copied for this rewrite, so no new provenance
entry is needed. The permitted alternatives were checked and rejected on
technical grounds, not licensing:

- CUTLASS (including the BSD-3 `include/cutlass` tree) — excluded by the task
  constraint against vendoring the whole package; its GEMM would also have
  replaced, not informed, the slice's own kernels.
- vLLM / SuperInfer `csrc/*` (Apache-2.0) — their dense GEMM paths are CUTLASS
  or cuBLAS wrappers, and the remaining files (layernorm, activation, rotary,
  cache) cover operators that are under 0.5% of this model's runtime; copying
  them would add provenance surface with no measured gain.
- FlashAttention-style prefill attention — not adopted; measured attention
  cost is 0.2% of prefill and 0.1% of decode here (see OMNI_NATIVE.md).


## Specifications derived from upstream reference code (read-only)

All model math, tensor names/shapes, the Qwen2 tokenizer algorithm, image
preprocessing, multimodal RoPE and the MoE routing rules were derived by
reading these Apache-2.0 sources on the reference host. No upstream source
code was copied into this directory; the C++/CUDA implementation was written
from scratch against the derived specifications.

- HuggingFace Transformers 5.6.0,
  `transformers/models/qwen3_omni_moe/`:
  - `modeling_qwen3_omni_moe.py` (generated model implementation)
  - `tokenization_qwen2.py` (Qwen2 byte-level BPE tokenizer)
  - `processing_qwen3_omni_moe.py` (image placeholder expansion)
- `transformers/models/qwen2_vl/image_processing_qwen2_vl.py`
  (smart_resize, antialias bicubic resize, patch reorder)
- SGLang `qwen3_omni_moe.py` (weight-name mapping and checkpoint loading
  cross-check only; the runtime is not linked or invoked)

## Generated Unicode tables

`unicode_ranges.hpp` is generated by `../omni_tests/gen_unicode_ranges.py`
from the Unicode 14.0 property database shipped with the build host's
Python (unicodedata). It contains compact codepoint ranges for the Letter,
Number and White_Space properties used by the Qwen2 pre-tokenization regex.
Regenerate with: `python3 gen_unicode_ranges.py > ../omni/unicode_ranges.hpp`.

## Skipped normalization and its ceiling

The Qwen2 tokenizer applies Unicode NFC before BPE. This implementation
skips NFC (see the ponytail comment in `tokenizer.cpp`); all prompts used by
the slice are already NFC and the HF golden vectors in the test suite pass.
A mini Unicode composer is the documented upgrade if non-NFC input appears.

## Runtime boundary

The `umm-omni-native` binary links only the CUDA runtime. It does not link
or invoke Python, PyTorch, torchvision, vLLM, SGLang or cuBLAS. Verified with
`ldd` on the GPU host. The `omni_gemm.cu` kernels use only PTX tensor-core and
`cp.async` instructions; no library GEMM is called.
